 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“Whereas some doubts have arisen whether children got by any Englishman upon a negro woman should be slave or [free], Be it therefore enacted and declared by this present grand assembly, that all children borne in this country [shall be] held bond or free only according to the condition of the mother, And that if any christian shall [commit fornication] with a negro man or woman, [he or she so] offending shall pay double the [fines] imposed by the former act (Hening 1809–23 Vol 2:170).</p>\n<p>[Under English law a child received his or her status from his father. This Virginia colonial law of December 1662 made a child of an enslaved mother a slave for life.]”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Enactment of Hereditary Slavery Law Virginia 1662-ACT XII</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided</i>.</p>\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614783,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "According to the 1662 law in the excerpt provided, what is the status of the child of an enslaved mother and an Englishman in Virginia?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167105,
     "content_html": "The child was born a free child."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167104,
     "content_html": "The child had to be emancipated by age 21 years."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167106,
     "content_html": "The child was born a slave."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167103,
     "content_html": "The child had the full rights of an Englishman."
    }
   ],
